From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:10:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: cancel negative-duration interaction boosts

IPower.setBoost specifies that a negative duration cancels the previous
boost. InteractionHandler currently clamps it to the minimum duration,
starting or extending a boost instead.

Handle cancellation under the existing state lock. Abort an outstanding
display-idle wait, return an initialized handler to idle, and release the
INTERACTION vote. Keep the uninitialized timed-fallback state unchanged.
Other hints retain their own votes through libperfmgr.

Base: 13281f8a0d718205781245f27ded74bc5ff03388
Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_hardware_lineage_interfaces/blob/13281f8a0d718205781245f27ded74bc5ff03388/power-libperfmgr/aidl/InteractionHandler.cpp
Contract: hardware/interfaces/power/aidl/android/hardware/power/IPower.aidl
Signed-off-by: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
---
 power-libperfmgr/aidl/InteractionHandler.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/power-libperfmgr/aidl/InteractionHandler.cpp b/power-libperfmgr/aidl/InteractionHandler.cpp
--- a/power-libperfmgr/aidl/InteractionHandler.cpp
+++ b/power-libperfmgr/aidl/InteractionHandler.cpp
@@ -151,6 +151,17 @@ void InteractionHandler::Acquire(int32_t duration) {
 
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(mLock);
 
+    if (duration < 0) {
+        if (mState == INTERACTION_STATE_WAITING) {
+            AbortWaitLocked();
+        }
+        if (mState != INTERACTION_STATE_UNINITIALIZED) {
+            mState = INTERACTION_STATE_IDLE;
+        }
+        PerfRel();
+        return;
+    }
+
     int inputDuration = duration + kDurationOffsetMs;
     int finalDuration;
     if (inputDuration > kMaxDurationMs)
